1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,669
Notary. No certificate, no money moves.

2
00:00:04,136 --> 00:00:08,884
AI agents are starting to move real money:
refunds, plan changes, credits.

3
00:00:08,989 --> 00:00:10,963
They learn how from API docs.

4
00:00:11,381 --> 00:00:14,283
But docs and real APIs disagree.

5
00:00:14,956 --> 00:00:20,112
We pointed our agent at two real APIs,
Crustdata and Dodo Payments.

6
00:00:20,530 --> 00:00:25,023
Crustdata's own docs say a company lookup
with no match returns an empty result.

7
00:00:25,534 --> 00:00:30,642
In our run, it returned an error instead,
and three documented claims didn't hold.

8
00:00:30,886 --> 00:00:34,926
An agent that trusts the docs breaks on
exactly these cases.

9
00:00:35,387 --> 00:00:40,252
Notary is an agent that won't touch money
until it has proven how its tools behave.

10
00:00:40,635 --> 00:00:44,362
It reads the docs and turns every promise
into a claim.

11
00:00:44,803 --> 00:00:48,367
Before each test call, it commits a
prediction, hashed,

12
00:00:48,518 --> 00:00:50,422
so it can't change afterwards.

13
00:00:50,863 --> 00:00:53,313
Then it calls the API and compares.

14
00:00:53,754 --> 00:00:56,087
A Reflector proposes explanations.

15
00:00:56,366 --> 00:01:00,731
A stronger Adversary, running on a
different model, tries to refute them.

16
00:01:01,173 --> 00:01:05,874
In our runs, it narrowed all five beliefs
instead of rubber-stamping them.

17
00:01:06,316 --> 00:01:10,542
What survives becomes a certificate, valid
only where it was tested.

18
00:01:10,983 --> 00:01:12,248
And the rule is simple.

19
00:01:12,690 --> 00:01:15,255
No certificate, no money moves.

20
00:01:15,638 --> 00:01:19,597
The Guard holds anything uncovered for a
person to review.

21
00:01:20,065 --> 00:01:24,848
Dodo Payments is where the money moves:
refunds, credits and plan changes,

22
00:01:25,057 --> 00:01:26,590
run in test mode.

23
00:01:27,286 --> 00:01:31,176
Notary certified four Dodo behaviors
before trusting them,

24
00:01:31,350 --> 00:01:35,762
from page limits to wallet credit units
and idempotency keys.

25
00:01:36,575 --> 00:01:41,660
Crustdata tells the agent who each
customer is, so the right policy applies.

26
00:01:41,985 --> 00:01:44,760
The models run through a LiteLLM gateway,

27
00:01:44,969 --> 00:01:47,546
with Claude as the Reflector and
Adversary.

28
00:01:47,929 --> 00:01:54,907
And Notary is built to run on AWS: deploy
scripts for a read-only hosted API on ECS,

29
00:01:55,081 --> 00:01:58,065
and Amazon Bedrock as a drop-in model
provider,

30
00:01:58,216 --> 00:02:03,533
so the agents and their models can run
inside a team's own AWS account.

31
00:02:03,985 --> 00:02:06,771
We used neatlogs to look inside every run.

32
00:02:07,155 --> 00:02:13,261
Each run is one trace: every probe, every
model call, every guard decision,

33
00:02:13,470 --> 00:02:14,817
labelled by agent.

34
00:02:15,258 --> 00:02:19,752
On the Crustdata run, the trace shows the
probe for one disputed claim.

35
00:02:20,193 --> 00:02:24,477
Its prediction is logged, with its hash,
before the call is made.

36
00:02:24,802 --> 00:02:29,748
The result came back inconclusive, so
Notary resolved it the safe way:

37
00:02:30,131 --> 00:02:34,229
it abstained, and no payment can depend on
that claim.

38
00:02:35,344 --> 00:02:40,417
Two more mismatches, lookups that error
where the docs promise an empty result,

39
00:02:40,568 --> 00:02:41,660
are still open.

40
00:02:42,170 --> 00:02:46,814
Notary hasn't certified them, so the Guard
won't let money depend on them either.

41
00:02:47,627 --> 00:02:52,805
On the Dodo run, the trace shows the
Adversary narrowing four beliefs instead

42
00:02:52,851 --> 00:02:54,442
of upholding them as written.

43
00:02:54,953 --> 00:02:59,109
Wallet credits, for example, are in minor
units only for US dollars.

44
00:02:59,550 --> 00:03:04,589
Notary resolved those by certifying only
the narrower scope it had proven.

45
00:03:05,041 --> 00:03:07,467
Entire captured how Notary was built.

46
00:03:07,851 --> 00:03:12,297
Seven checkpoints tie each commit to the
coding-agent session that wrote it.

47
00:03:12,738 --> 00:03:17,673
Notary also uses Entire's code graph to
prove a safety property:

48
00:03:18,114 --> 00:03:21,411
every call that can move money goes
through a guard.

49
00:03:21,736 --> 00:03:24,128
Zero unguarded call sites.

50
00:03:24,589 --> 00:03:29,779
And Notary measures what certainty costs:
about three cents of model spend and

51
00:03:29,860 --> 00:03:32,124
fifteen Crustdata credits per run.

52
00:03:32,565 --> 00:03:37,917
It exports those numbers for cfo.ai to
build the business plan on.

53
00:03:38,390 --> 00:03:40,422
So here is what Notary proved.

54
00:03:40,747 --> 00:03:43,278
Three documented claims that didn't hold.

55
00:03:43,522 --> 00:03:47,179
Five certificates, each one narrowed by
the Adversary.

56
00:03:47,504 --> 00:03:51,289
Zero unguarded money calls, at about three
cents a run.

57
00:03:51,730 --> 00:03:55,759
Notary. No certificate, no money moves.
